{
    "word": "cruet",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7c29c1ce-faa2-3b58-ab45-53cd24e094ae",
                "word": "cruet",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3ccc6a89-545e-4748-95b5-7defa5c856df",
                        "entry_id": "7c29c1ce-faa2-3b58-ab45-53cd24e094ae",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cruets"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "52fe75c5-6ff0-3bc3-afe6-b8573280e76a",
                        "entry_id": "7c29c1ce-faa2-3b58-ab45-53cd24e094ae",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small bottle or container used to hold a condiment, such as salt, pepper, oil, or vinegar, for use at a dining table."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c454658d-8294-4bc1-8176-755f130e89d4",
                                "sense_id": "52fe75c5-6ff0-3bc3-afe6-b8573280e76a",
                                "text": "\"By Jupiter there's vinegar!\" I heard him say to his friend, after he had stood on tiptoe an immense time, and had been crushed and beaten on all sides. \"And there's oil!! I saw them distinctly, in cruets! Can any gentleman, in front there, see mustard on the table? Sir, will you oblige me! Do you see a Mustard-Pot?\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6bc4829-b176-452a-837b-c3110f80ec2b",
                                "sense_id": "52fe75c5-6ff0-3bc3-afe6-b8573280e76a",
                                "text": "The sideboard was covered with glistening old plate—old cups, both gold and silver; old salvers and cruet-stands, like Rundell and Bridge's shop."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "396ecf68-738b-46e3-a112-98bfac0bf527",
                                "sense_id": "52fe75c5-6ff0-3bc3-afe6-b8573280e76a",
                                "text": "Mrs. Hussey soon appeared, with a mustard-pot in one hand and a vinegar-cruet in the other, having just broken away from the occupation of attending to the castors, and scolding her little black boy meantime."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f20ace6d-367e-49e7-b524-6227ff916675",
                                "sense_id": "52fe75c5-6ff0-3bc3-afe6-b8573280e76a",
                                "text": "It must always be done at night, so that Jurgis could go along; and even if it were only a pepper cruet, or half a dozen glasses for ten cents, that was enough for an expedition."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2cce0f91-6d92-3d78-b47b-a6b4caa09ac4",
                        "entry_id": "7c29c1ce-faa2-3b58-ab45-53cd24e094ae",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A stand for these containers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "85d38b43-66a5-4665-a079-e2d99cf295ac",
                                "sense_id": "2cce0f91-6d92-3d78-b47b-a6b4caa09ac4",
                                "text": "He[…]even had a second slice of lamb, for he was hungry. During the meal, as was his custom, he read from a book propped up against the cruet."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f099fe69-00f9-3c73-bf3f-90a4e780b6c0",
